---
const faqs = [
  {
    question:
      "Should we build a mobile app or a responsive website?",
    answer:
      "That depends on how people need to use the service. If the experience is occasional and primarily informational, a responsive website may be enough. Repeated use, notifications, offline capability or device-specific features can make an app more appropriate.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can one application work on both Android and iOS?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Cross-platform frameworks can share a significant portion of the codebase across Android and iOS. Whether that approach is suitable depends on functionality, performance and platform-specific requirements.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can the app connect to our existing software?",
    answer:
      "Usually, if the existing system exposes suitable APIs or can be extended safely. Integration requirements should be reviewed before mobile development begins.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can you build the backend as well as the mobile app?",
    answer:
      "Yes. LKProfessionals can develop APIs, authentication, data services, administrative systems and other backend components required by the application.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Do mobile apps need ongoing maintenance?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Mobile operating systems, store policies, dependencies, device behaviour and backend services change over time.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can LKP help publish the app?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Release preparation can include production configuration and assistance with the relevant store submission process, subject to the customer's required developer accounts and platform policies.",
  },
];
---

<section class="mobile-faq">
  <div class="site-container mobile-faq__layout">
    <div>
      <p>Mobile app development FAQ</p>

      <h2>
        Questions before committing to the app.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="mobile-faq__list">
      {
        faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .mobile-faq {
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .mobile-faq__layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(16rem, 0.68fr)
      minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 8rem);
  }

  .mobile-faq__layout
    > div:first-child > p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #0b2f8f;
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .mobile-faq h2 {
    max-width: 11ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: #0d203c;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.6rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .mobile-faq__list {
    border-top: 1px solid #dce3ec;
  }

  .mobile-faq details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #dce3ec;
    padding-block: 1rem;
  }

  .mobile-faq summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: #293b53;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 740;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .mobile-faq details p {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    color: #788497;
    font-size: 0.69rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .mobile-faq__layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
